From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: mask the HFI interrupt before booting the GMU

GMU2HOST_INTR_MASK reads 0 after the GMU power domain was off, and
a6xx_gmu_resume() only programs it after a6xx_hfi_start(). Until then
every HFI response raises the HFI interrupt line. The interrupt is
disabled at that point, but lazily, so nearly every resume delivers it
once and the flow handler masks and drops it.

When the target CPU is in an idle state that is slow to leave, the
delivery can arrive after enable_irq(). a6xx_hfi_irq() then runs for an
interrupt whose status was cleared and masked before, right while
a6xx_gmu_set_initial_freq() and the GPU_SET OOB request are waiting for
their own bits in the same register.

Mask everything before the GMU boots. The write after a6xx_hfi_start()
still unmasks the CM3 fault.

[ARMDeck: Nova-Deck kernel/patches/0260 (from Armada 0622). Preventive,
with 0020. Software only. Compile-tested only as of 2026-10-27 (test
image r17).]
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 42f75c996..2a09c5713 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -1095,6 +1095,9 @@ int a6xx_gmu_resume(struct a6xx_gpu *a6xx_gpu)
 	/* Set the bus quota to a reasonable value for boot */
 	a6xx_gmu_set_initial_bw(gpu, gmu);
 
+	/* The mask resets to 0 with the GMU: keep HFI replies off the irq line */
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_MASK, ~0);
+
 	/* Enable the GMU interrupt */
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_CLR, ~0);
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_MASK, ~A6XX_GMU_IRQ_MASK);
